  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-03T16:39:51.067Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Not sure if there is a Canny for this already, but personally I found it very difficult to manage roles for the group I have.\n\nThe problem is that, there is no convenient way to see what roles a user has, there is no way to filter users by role and the member list isn't organized by roles either (like having users with moderation listed higher).\n\nUsing Discord for comparison, they make it easier to manage roles. The members list shows you every role assigned to a user in a list without needing to inspect each user individually. You can filter members by their role. Outside of that, the userlist on the side of the chat can also have members sorted by their role, with owner top, moderation second, other roles of significance after that, and then everyone else (just example). It makes it much easier to see who is what and something like moderation and admins I would want to be higher up in the list.\n\nIn my case, I wanted to add a \"Verified\" role for people that I knew from VRC / Discord / Twitter ect who I know aren't random bot or troll accounts, but I quickly found out that it would be tedious to manage as I had no way of knowing if everyone who was supposed to have the role actually had the role.",
